# Development hosting plan

Deploy the existing NestJS Docker application in Singapore in rg-jaj-dev-sea.
Use one Consumption replica (0.25 vCPU, 0.5 GiB), a Basic private container
registry, Key Vault references via an application managed identity, and
Log Analytics with 30-day retention. A delegated subnet with a NAT gateway
provides one fixed outbound address to allowlist in the existing PostgreSQL
and Event Hubs firewalls. Preserve the developer firewall rules.

Use Bicep under infra/, validate and preview changes before each deployment.
Build and smoke-test the Linux AMD64 image locally, push it, then deploy the
application with health probes on port 3000. Verify HTTPS health and Kafka
connectivity. The existing development restaurant database remains the app DB.
No production hosting is included.

Create a separate GitHub deployment identity resource group and bind its OIDC
federated credential to the repository's testing environment. Grant only
registry push and target-app deployment permissions. GitHub admin access is
needed to activate the environment settings and CI/CD workflows.
